# secrets
.env

# node
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# swift
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.o

# The assembled app bundle. Rebuilt by `make bundle` from sources that ARE
# tracked, so committing it only churns a 1MB binary on every build — and a
# stale committed copy is worse than none, since it is what `open build/Deiko.app`
# would launch.
build/

# Captured content — never commit crops, audio, transcripts or probe logs.
# These carry whatever was on screen: DB ids, tokens, customer data, scrollback.
#
# Matched by PATTERN, not just by directory: a probe log written to the wrong
# folder is still a leak, and that is exactly how ax-poked.jsonl reached a
# commit. Anything ignored here is ignored wherever it lands.
sessions/
*.jsonl
crops/
*.wav
# Crops are screenshots of whatever was on screen, and both crop destinations
# are user-settable (`capture --out`, `ax-probe --crop-dir`) — so the pattern,
# not just the folders.
*.png
# The landing site IS source imagery, and it is the one thing the pattern above
# swallows silently: the icon and the OG image would deploy fine from the machine
# that built them and 404 for everyone who clones. Narrow exception on purpose —
# a stray crop landing anywhere else in the repo is still ignored.
!site/assets/*.png

# The design hand-off from Claude Design: the zip and the folder it unpacks to.
# Neither is source. The site in `site/` is what was built from it and that is
# what ships; this is the working copy of the artboards, kept locally as
# reference for the ad and shot-list work. 13MB of screen recordings, a music
# bed and a dozen mood-board JPEGs do not belong in every clone forever, and
# the canvas is the real home of the originals.
*.zip
mddocs/design/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# stamped at deploy time by scripts/deploy-site.sh
site/install.sh

# wrangler pages dev scratch — also what made `make release` see a dirty tree
.wrangler/
graphify-out/
